# Hand-written rules that Astro's `redirects` map cannot express. The Cloudflare
# adapter appends the generated rules below these at build time.
#
# Astro writes every redirect source with a trailing slash (trailingSlash:
# 'always'), so `/index.htm` is emitted as `/index.htm/`. The host adds the
# slash itself for an extensionless path, but not for one that looks like a
# file, so the old WordPress `.htm` addresses still 404ed after
# stonesteps-50k#158 (checked live 2026-10-25). Exact matches here, one hop.
# The slashed forms stay in src/lib/launch-redirects.ts.
/index.htm                      /   301
/index_files/Registration.htm   /   301
